        "note": "The raw ci8 stream carries a rectangular gain step locked to an 8192-sample period: samples 0-895 of every period are 0.431 dB lower in power than samples 896-8191, flat either side of the step. It is stream-wide, not signal-specific - it shows in the wideband total power, on the receiver's own DC line (27 dB comb) and the 10 MHz reference harmonic (16 dB), and in bands with no emission at all (23 dB at 100.150 MHz). It puts a comb at 292.969 Hz (= 2.4 MHz / 8192) and its harmonics into the amplitude and, through the filter, the discriminator of anything narrowband and weak, with the sinc nulls of a 896/8192 duty cycle near harmonics 9 and 18. Anything looking for periodicity, frame rates or cyclostationarity in this fixture must exclude n * 292.969 Hz; taken at face value it reads as a 3.41 ms TDMA frame that is not there. Source not identified - it is present in the 2026-09-13 2.4 Msps capture of the same device as well."
      }
